    "canonicalImportReview": "voice_gateway.go and voice_transport.go retain the original github.com/bwmarrin/discordgo/internal/dave imports instead of the published fork namespace. These import-only changes update the active source hashes; upstream-base identity and historical baseline/audit records are unchanged. discordgo/ source identities remain stable inventory labels, not prepared-generation paths.",
    "publicationSourceReview": "Historical published v0.30.0 incorporated gofmt doc-comment layout changes in logging.go and oauth2.go; its five reviewed Application method documentation fingerprints followed those comments without changing signatures, bodies, defaults or classifications. The maintained patch stack excludes those comment-only reflows and the active fingerprints now follow the original upstream comment layout. voice.go remains byte-identical to the reviewed published source and main commit 3158838b78dd92cb8220673cc4887d009204ef1a. Historical snapshots and audits remain unchanged.",
    "retirementSourceReview": "The published voice.go matches existing main source but active inventories lagged its retirement handshake. VoiceConnection.leaveAck and leaveConfirmed are private runtime-only state: ordered null-channel observation closes the acknowledgement; DisconnectContext waits within CloseTimeout, joins confirmation errors, and retains the reservation until cleanup and confirmation. Two extra anonymous empty struct channel types are implementation-local. Other nested identity changes and public declaration fingerprints are source-position shifts plus the separately reviewed OAuth documentation formatting; no module exposure changes.",
